module vid-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

import core.authority.{ CaseOrder }
import core.frcrimp45.{ frcrimp45 }

// The District Court of the Virgin Islands' own criminal periods, counted
// under the criminal rules (FRCrimP 45(a) governs "any local rule"). No
// trigger carries a service method.
//
// Conditions that are not deadlines from a party's event stay in notes: by
// arraignment on a superseding charge, defense counsel states whether the
// defendant agrees that it starts a new trial clock (D.V.I. LRCr 7.1(b));
// the parties may extend by agreement the deadline for a complex-case
// motion (LRCr 12.6(c)); leave to exceed the 5-page or 1,500-word limit on
// a motion to modify discovery, its response or reply is sought at least
// two days before filing (LRCr 16.1(f)(1)); and a Rule 17(c) subpoena may
// not require production in fewer than 14 days after service absent good
// cause (LRCr 17.2(d)), a minimum rather than a deadline. Pro se
// defendants are outside the LRCr 16.1(a) conference and the joint
// discovery statement; the Court sets their discovery deadlines (LRCr
// 16.1(a)(4), (h)). The Speedy Trial Act Plan (LRCr 55.2) is not vendored.
//
// The earlier D.V.I. criminal outline's FRCrimP flow and its decisions are
// FRCrimP, Speedy Trial Act or constitutional authority and belong to
// lit/frcrimp; they are removed here: no reporter text is vendored.
/// What starts the government's default Rule 16(a) production period (LRCr
/// 16.1(b)): arraignment, for a written request made at or before it, or
/// a written request made after arraignment.
enum GovernmentDiscoveryStart { Arraignment, LaterRequest }

/// The arraignment on the first information or indictment, or a written
/// Rule 16 request made after it (D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(b): the period runs
/// from the later, the most recent of these events).
event GovernmentDiscoveryClock(start: GovernmentDiscoveryStart)

/// What starts a defendant's default Rule 16(b) production period (LRCr
/// 16.1(c)): the government's written request, or the government's own
/// deadline under the corresponding subsection of Rule 16(a).
enum DefendantDiscoveryStart { GovernmentRequest, GovernmentDeadline }

/// The government's Rule 16 request, or the government's corresponding
/// Rule 16(a) deadline (D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(c): the later, the most recent of
/// these events).
event DefendantDiscoveryClock(start: DefendantDiscoveryStart)
/// The defendant is arraigned on the first information or indictment
/// filed as to the defendant (D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(a)(1)).
event ArraignedOnFirstCharge()
/// The initial discovery conference is completed (D.V.I. LRCr 12.6(a),
/// 16.1(a)(2)).
event DiscoveryConferenceCompleted()
/// The government's deadline to provide Rule 16 discovery arrives (D.V.I.
/// LRCr 12.6(b), 16.1(d)(2)).
event GovernmentDiscoveryDue()
/// The defendant is arraigned on a new information or indictment in the
/// same case (D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(d)).
event ArraignedOnSupersedingCharge()
/// A motion for a continuance of trial is served (D.V.I. LRCr 12.5(c)).
event ContinuanceMotionServed()
/// A motion to modify the time, place or manner of discovery is served
/// (D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(f)(2)).
event DiscoveryModificationMotionServed()
/// A response to a motion to modify discovery is served (D.V.I. LRCr
/// 16.1(f)(2)).
event DiscoveryModificationResponseServed()
/// Trial is set to commence (D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(h)).
event TrialCommencement()
/// A court appearance for which an interpreter's services are required,
/// other than a preliminary proceeding (D.V.I. LRCr 28.1).
event InterpretedAppearance()

/// D.V.I. LRCr 12.5(c)(2): a party opposing a motion for a continuance of
/// trial files a memorandum in opposition within seven days after service
/// of the motion, unless the Court sets a shorter period; a party that
/// files none is deemed not to oppose it (LRCr 12.5(c)(3)).
deadline continuance-opposition: 7.days after ContinuanceMotionServed() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D.V.I. LRCr 12.5(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCr 12.6(a): the government moves for complex-case designation
/// before the initial discovery conference begins, and a defendant files
/// a written response, agreeing or opposing with reasons, no later than
/// seven days after the conference. The Court may extend it for good
/// cause (LRCr 12.6(c)).
deadline complex-designation-response: 7.days after DiscoveryConferenceCompleted() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D.V.I. LRCr 12.6(a); D.V.I. LRCr 12.6(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCr 12.6(b): a defendant seeking complex-case designation files
/// a written motion no later than five days after the government's
/// deadline to provide Rule 16 discovery. The Court may extend it for good
/// cause, and the parties by agreement (LRCr 12.6(c)).
deadline defendant-complex-designation: 5.days after GovernmentDiscoveryDue() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D.V.I. LRCr 12.6(b); D.V.I. LRCr 12.6(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(a)(1): unless otherwise ordered, no later than 14 days
/// after the arraignment on the first information or indictment, counsel
/// for the government and the defendant confer and try to agree on a
/// timetable and procedures for Rule 16 disclosure.
deadline initial-discovery-conference: 14.days after ArraignedOnFirstCharge() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(a)(2): within five days of the completion of the
/// conference, the parties file a notice of proposed pretrial discovery
/// timetable stating every agreed deadline; its deadlines bind the parties
/// unless the Court modifies them (LRCr 16.1(a)(3)).
deadline discovery-timetable-notice: 5.days after DiscoveryConferenceCompleted() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(b): unless the Court sets a different deadline, a
/// party moves for complex-case designation, or the parties' timetable
/// notice says otherwise, the government satisfies its Rule 16(a)
/// obligation on a written request within 28 days of a request made after
/// arraignment, or 28 days after arraignment for a request made at or
/// before it.
deadline government-rule16: 28.days after GovernmentDiscoveryClock() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(c): on the same conditions, a defendant satisfies a
/// Rule 16(b) obligation on the government's written request within the
/// later of 14 days after the request or 14 days after the government's
/// deadline under the corresponding subsection of Rule 16(a).
deadline defendant-rule16: 14.days after DefendantDiscoveryClock() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(d)(1): a defendant's earlier discovery request applies
/// to a new information or indictment in the same case unless the
/// defendant files a notice limiting it within one day of the arraignment
/// on the new charge.
deadline superseding-request-limit: 1.days after ArraignedOnSupersedingCharge() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(d)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(d)(2): unless the Court sets a different deadline or a
/// party moves for complex-case designation, the government satisfies its
/// Rule 16(a) obligation under a prior request no later than 14 days after
/// arraignment on the new information or indictment.
deadline superseding-government-rule16: 14.days after ArraignedOnSupersedingCharge() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(d)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(d)(2): the defendant satisfies a Rule 16(b) obligation
/// under a prior request no later than 7 days after the government's
/// deadline under the corresponding subsection of Rule 16(a).
deadline superseding-defendant-rule16: 7.days after GovernmentDiscoveryDue() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(d)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(f)(2): a response to a motion to modify the time,
/// place or manner of discovery is filed within three business days after
/// service of the motion.
deadline discovery-modification-response: 3.business_days after DiscoveryModificationMotionServed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(f)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(f)(2): a reply is filed within three business days
/// after service of the response.
deadline discovery-modification-reply: 3.business_days after DiscoveryModificationResponseServed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(f)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(h): counsel for the government and the defendant file
/// a signed Joint Discovery Statement, describing the discovery exchanged
/// and setting out all stipulations, no later than seven days before the
/// commencement of every trial, or when the Court directs.
deadline joint-discovery-statement: 7.days before TrialCommencement() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D.V.I. LRCr 16.1(h)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D.V.I. LRCr 28.1: except in preliminary proceedings, every request for
/// interpreting services is made to the Court at least seven days before
/// the interpreter's services are required.
deadline interpreter-request: 7.days before InterpretedAppearance() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D.V.I. LRCr 28.1"
{
  forum frcrimp
}
